"""Reviewed fixed Kanto object descriptions; no menu prompts or inferred outcomes."""
ROWS=[]
def add(key,label,subject,lines):
    replies=[s.strip() for s in lines.split('|')]
    assert len(replies)==11,(key,len(replies))
    ROWS.append(dict(key='kanto_object_'+key,labels=[label],subject=subject,replies=replies))

add('program','CeladonCity_Condominiums_3F_Text_ItsTheGameProgram','The computer holds game code; the description warns that changing it could introduce bugs.',
"I have touched enough buttons today. This one can remain mysterious.|An untested edit could affect much more than the line we change. Leave their work intact.|Their work. Their keyboard. Hands off.|A wrong note is easy to hear. A wrong instruction might wait hours to hurt something.|Do not season somebody else's recipe while they are away from the stove.|The world's least welcoming guest book. Sensible, really.|A tiny mistake waiting to become everyone's afternoon.|Interesting system. Inspection permission does not include permission to modify it.|Some spells deserve the courtesy of being left exactly as written.|Imagine coming back from lunch and finding a stranger has improved your job.|I would rather ask how they made it than find out how easily I can break it.")
add('playing_at_work','CeladonCity_Condominiums_3F_Text_SomeonesPlayingGame','A developer is playing a game instead of working.',
"Maybe this is research. I would also like a job with suspiciously enjoyable research.|Playing can reveal design problems. The description does suggest this is a break, though.|Let them have five minutes. We just walked into their office.|You can learn a lot by listening to somebody else's song. Also, sometimes you just like it.|Taste the food before serving it. This may be a very long tasting.|A convincing disguise for avoiding work: do something almost related to it.|The deadline cannot see them if they remain perfectly still.|Could be a useful comparison. Could also be a spectacularly good distraction.|Even diligent hands sometimes wander toward a little joy.|We are staring at their screen. We have become the office problem.|I wonder which part they keep coming back to. That usually tells you something.")
add('script_ending','CeladonCity_Condominiums_3F_Text_ItsScriptBetterNotLookAtEnding','A script is on the desk; the player decides against reading its ending.',
"Good. I like arriving at surprises with my eyebrows unprepared.|Knowing the conclusion would change how we interpret every earlier scene.|Close it before one sentence ruins a whole adventure.|I want the last note to mean something when we finally hear it.|No dessert before dinner. Even if the dessert has a very tempting title.|A fellow writer's ending, undefended on a desk. We shall exercise immense restraint.|Let the future retain at least one locked drawer.|Respect the intended sequence. And their unpublished draft.|An unopened ending still has room to surprise us.|Absolutely no reading the last page. I need to worry in the correct order.|I would rather remember how we reached the ending than just what happened.")
add('super_nes','CeladonCity_DepartmentStore_3F_Text_ItsSuperNES','A Super NES console is on display in the game shop.',
"It is like a tiny adventure machine. Much less walking than our usual arrangement.|A whole set of rules inside one box. I can see the appeal.|Looks fun. We should finish what we came here for first.|I wonder what its music sounds like through the shop speakers.|Does it come with snacks, or is that a separate department?|A heroic quest with a chair included. A formidable competitor.|A small box promising to consume a large evening.|The controller is a neat solution to having far too few hands inside the screen.|A window to somewhere else, with a cord to remind you to come back.|We could lose an entire rainy afternoon to that. I mean that fondly.|People must remember their first games the way we remember our first routes.")
add('rpg','CeladonCity_DepartmentStore_3F_Text_AnRPG','The player notices an RPG but says there is no time to play.',
"Another adventure? My adventure pockets are already full.|We have limited time and several unfinished obligations. Sensible restraint.|One journey at a time. Ours still needs us.|It can wait. A good story will still be there when we have room to listen.|Starting another long commitment while hungry is how dinner becomes tomorrow.|A quest inside a quest. At last, a way to be behind on two destinies.|We have enough unfinished business without buying it in a box.|Scope control. An unexpectedly difficult skill in a game shop.|Leave that road unwalked for now. It will keep.|I want it. I also want us to arrive somewhere before the shop closes.|Maybe later we can compare its idea of traveling with the real thing.")
add('puzzle_game','CeladonCity_DepartmentStore_3F_Text_PuzzleGame','A puzzle game looks likely to be addictive.',
"Just one more round is a very suspicious sentence. It always brings friends.|A clear goal and immediate feedback can make stopping surprisingly difficult.|Decide when to stop before you start. Easier that way.|I would keep thinking about the unfinished pattern after putting it down.|That has the same danger as tasting one more spoonful until the pot is empty.|An innocent little puzzle, applying for ownership of our evening.|A neat arrangement of pieces. A less neat arrangement of tomorrow's sleep.|Simple rules can produce excellent problems. I respect that design.|A little knot asking to be untied. Then another knot. Then dawn.|We would both say one round and both know we were lying.|I like seeing the instant somebody notices the solution. Their whole face changes.")
add('vending_success','CeladonCity_DepartmentStore_Roof_Text_DrinkCanPoppedOut','The vending machine successfully dispenses the selected drink.',
"It worked! A tiny metal waiter with excellent boundaries.|Payment accepted and the chosen drink delivered. A reassuringly clear transaction.|Drink secured. Keep the empty can until we find a bin.|That little clunk is a surprisingly satisfying sound.|Excellent. Now we can stop pretending thirst is a personality.|The machine has fulfilled its entire character arc in one clunk.|A cold drink emerging from a warm afternoon. A modest miracle.|One input, one correct output. I wish every machine behaved that well.|The rooftop has offered a small, cold kindness.|That was the sound of us becoming slightly easier to travel with.|A quick drink and a look at the city. I like this stop.")
add('vending_full','CeladonCity_DepartmentStore_Roof_Text_NoMoreRoomForStuff','The vending purchase cannot fit because the bag is full.',
"The bag has voted against hydration. We should reorganize the committee.|The purchase needs free storage space. Sorting the bag is the useful next step.|Make room first. No reason to keep feeding the machine.|There is something very sad about being this close to a cold drink.|We packed for every emergency except wanting a beverage.|Our expedition has been defeated by the dimensions of a can.|The smallest obstacle today is also, apparently, insurmountable.|Capacity limit reached. Move something before attempting another purchase.|A crowded bag has shut the door on a very small comfort.|We are carrying an entire lifestyle and have nowhere to put a drink.|This is a good moment to check what we have been carrying without using.")
add('vending_money','CeladonCity_DepartmentStore_Roof_Text_NotEnoughMoney','The vending purchase fails because the player lacks enough money.',
"It is being very firm about the part where we pay it.|The displayed price exceeds our funds. Another attempt will not change that.|Count what we have before choosing again.|A cold drink would be nice. We can manage without buying one right now.|We should save the coins we have for what we actually need.|A machine immune to charm. A chilling adversary even without the drink.|The thirst remains. The money also remains, technically.|Insufficient funds is a clear answer. No amount of button pressing revises it.|Some doors open with coins. This one can remain closed for now.|We can leave without making being short on money into a whole performance.|Let us find a place to rest anyway. Buying something need not be the price of a pause.")
add('blaine_fuji_photo','CinnabarIsland_Gym_Text_PhotoOfBlaineAndFuji','A photograph shows Blaine and Mr. Fuji smiling together.',
"They look like they were having a really good day. I am glad somebody kept it.|The photograph shows a friendship, not just two names we know separately.|Good picture. They look comfortable together.|Those smiles feel less formal than the ones people save for portraits.|I hope there was a good meal somewhere on that day.|A glimpse of people before we met them in their official roles.|Even people with difficult histories have days worth keeping.|Useful reminder that a person's life extends beyond the role we see.|A bright moment, kept where the years cannot quite reach it.|That is the kind of smile you get around someone who knows your embarrassing stories.|Someone chose to keep this friendship visible. I like that.")
